  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/75c9e43b1eae631c",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Josh-Alcantra-Headshot-2026_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Josh Alcantara"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Jersey Boys, Beautiful, White Christmas, Rock of Ages, Shrek (Drayton Entertainment); Footloose (Stage West); Joseph (Tweed&amp;Co); Sunday in the Park, Kiss of the Spider Woman (Eclipse Theatre); Mamma Mia! (Theatre St. Johns); Newsies (Theatre Sheridan).\r\n\r\nTRAINING: Bachelor of Music Theatre Performance (Sheridan College).\r\n\r\nFrom Kanata, Ontario, Josh is a professionally trained ballet dancer, independent songwriter/producer (JPA), and videographer (JPA Studios).\r\n\r\n&ldquo;Thank you to my friends and family, to Stephen and Nicole at daCosta Talent, and to my Kale, for your endless love and support. I&rsquo;ve been looking forward to working at the festival for a long time, and I&rsquo;m excited to be with this group of people and enjoy my first golden summer on the island! New JPA album coming this year!&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG &amp; TikTok: @joshpalcantara\r\n\r\nWEB: jpa-studios.com\r\n\r\n*UNDERSTUDY FOR: Moody MacPherson, Tommy Sloane, Charlie Sloane, Willie Boulter, Mr. Phillips, Cecil the Farmer, Earl the Mailman."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/f39a762e1bdb057e",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/LeShaun-Bernett-_-Headshot-2026.jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "LeShaun Bernett"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Jesus Christ Superstar (Drayton Entertainment).\r\n\r\nFILM/TV: RollPlay (Treehouse); 2018 Much Music Video Awards (iHeartRadio); Tiny Dancer (Unwrap Productions).\r\n\r\nTRAINING: BHSc from University of Ottawa and currently studies Pharmacology at the University of Toronto.\r\n\r\nHe is elated to make his Charlottetown Festival debut as Tommy Sloane in Anne of Green Gables—The Musical™! He is deeply honoured to step into the world of this iconic Canadian story and to bring its timeless characters to life. He thanks his dance teachers, vocal coach Caleb, friends, family, and his agents at 10 Talent Management for their unwavering support and mentorship that have guided him every step of the way.\r\n\r\nIG: @leshaunbernett"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/a5586f715f80afca",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/MALINDA-CARROLL-headshot_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Malinda Carroll"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nAnne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nRobin Hood (Canadian Stage); Waitress, 9-5 (Capitol Theatre); Lion of Oz (Tweed &amp; Co.); Rent, Richard II (Stratford Festival); Hairspray (Theatre Aquarius); Dear Evan Hansen (Mirvish); All Shook Up, Soul Sistas (Mayfield Dinner Theatre)\r\nTRAINING:\r\nMusic Theatre Performance (St. Clair College)\r\n\r\n&ldquo;The Confederation Centre is one of my favourite places to do theatre. I feel so grateful to have another golden summer!&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@malindacarroll_"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/915ae4f675bd626d",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Crystal-Casera-Headshot-2026_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Crystal Casera"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Disney&rsquo;s Frozen, The Sound of Music (Grand Theatre); The Frogs (Talk is Free Theatre); Heathers: The Musical (Theatre Sheridan); The SpongeBob Musical (Mansfield Entertainment).\r\n\r\nTRAINING: Bachelor of Music Theatre Performance Program (Sheridan College).\r\n\r\nCrystal is so excited to join the cast of Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;. She&rsquo;d like to thank her friends and family for all their love, support, and encouragement.\r\n\r\nIG: @caseraaa_"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/568d236cd991bed0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Micheline-Desaulniers-Headshot-2026_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Micheline Desaulniers"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\n\r\nTRAINING: BFA Performance Dance Program (Toronto Metropolitan University).\r\n\r\nA Toronto-based artist from Fredericton, NB, she has worked with artists including Louis Laberge-Côté, Pulga Muchochoma, and Susie Burpee. This production marks her first theatre and musical theatre experience, a fitting East Coast premiere with Anne. Love to her family, friends, and mentors.\r\n\r\n“I’m thrilled to bring Tillie to life and to understudy Josie Pye alongside such a talented cast and crew. Working on Anne of Green Gables—The Musical™ feels like coming home as an East Coaster, and I can’t wait to share this story with audiences.”\r\n\r\nIG: @michydesaulniers"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/80134a945b5ddf5a",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/MaAnne_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ma-Anne Dionisio"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDebut\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nThe Tale of the Gifted Prince (World Premiere) (Theatre Calgary); Miss Saigon (Canadian Premiere) (Princess of Wales Theatre); Les Misérables, Flower Drum Song, Martin Guerre, West Side Story, Mamma Mia!, Sunday in the Park with George, Grease, Jesus Christ Superstar, Cats (Broadway/London West End)\r\nOTHER:\r\nDora Award, ‘Diana’, Next to Normal (Mirvish/MusicalStageCo)\r\nFILM/TV (SELECT):\r\nThe Waiting Room (TimeLapse Pictures); In Her Mother’s Eyes (HERetic Films); Inang Reyna/Queen Mother (CFC/KingLouie Films); Mirabelle and Me (Bardel Entertainment/Nelvana); Schitt’s Creek (CBC); Remedy (Global); Flashpoint (CBS/CTV); Boston Blue (CBS); The Coroner (CBC)\r\nPhilippine-born Canadian actress Ma-Anne Dionisio is best known for portraying the role of “Kim” in the Canadian Premiere production of Miss Saigon at the Princess of Wales Theatre in Toronto."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/1df3b1199ae3e75d",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Tyler-Everley-Headshot-2026_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Tyler Everley"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Mary Poppins (Thousand Islands Playhouse); Shrek The Musical, Cinderella, The Little Mermaid, Mary Poppins (Rainbow Stage); 18 Palace Road, Something Rotten, Wild Child, Heathers (Theatre Sheridan).\r\n\r\nTRAINING: Bachelor of Music Theatre Performance Program (Sheridan College).\r\n\r\n&ldquo;Thank you to my friends and family for their endless support and the team at The Talent House for all you do. I am so excited to be joining the fantastic team bringing this beloved Canadian classic to life. I am honoured to get the chance to bring the role of Charlie Sloane to life alongside so many Canadian Theatre legends.&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG: @tyler.everley &nbsp; FB: Tyler Everley"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/5e1b22282e09353e",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/TaylorFlinders_Headshot_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Taylor Flinders"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Small Gods, Big Fish, Armchair Confidential, Heathers (Theatre Sheridan).\r\n\r\nFILM/TV: Dinosters &ndash; Animation (Funnyflux / Super Sonics Prods.).\r\n\r\nTRAINING: Graduate and Silver Medal Recipient, Bachelor of Music Theatre Performance and Performing Arts Preparation Program (Sheridan College).\r\n\r\n&ldquo;Thank you to my family, friends and the Talent House team for their incredible love and support; I wouldn&rsquo;t be here without all of you! I am so incredibly excited and grateful to be joining the world of Avonlea, and the beautiful legacy that is Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade; as Prissy; it&rsquo;s truly a dream come true. I look forward to working alongside this exceptional team and cast to bring this timeless show to life!&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG: @taylor.flinders\r\n\r\n*2ND COVER FOR: Gertie Pye, Ruby, Tillie Boulter, Tommy Sloane, Charlie Sloane, Willie Boulter."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/16e15fc0998fb386",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/JoemaFrith.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Joema Frith"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Disney’s The Lion King (Mirvish); Mary Poppins, Little Mermaid (Rainbow Stage); Beautiful: The Carole King Musical (Drayton Entertainment); Shrek: The Musical (YPT).\r\n\r\n“I am so excited to be joining the great legacy that is Anne of Green Gables—The Musical™ and getting to do it with so many friends makes it even better, and I can’t wait to bring this show to you. One day I’ll fulfill my dream of playing Anne but for now Gilbert will do. Thank you to my friends and family for the love and the team at Talent House for their constant support!”\r\n\r\nIG: @Joema_Frith"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/3ce2779e97832072",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Barbara-Fulerton-Headshot-2025_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Barbara Fulton"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: 4th Season. Anne of Green Gables—The Musical, Singin' &amp; Dancin’ TONIGHT, Ye Gods!, Johnny Belinda.\r\n\r\n  THEATRE (select): Come From Away, Toronto (Mirvish); Into The Woods, A Little Night Music, Fiddler on the Roof, The Sound of Music, The Lion, The Witch and The Wardrobe, A Midsummer Night’s Dream, Hamlet, The Merchant of Venice, Elektra, and more (The Stratford Festival, 22 seasons); Life After (Canadian Stage); Grizabella in CATS, original Canadian company, Toronto.\r\n\r\n  Originally from Nova Scotia, Barbara is thrilled to be on the East Coast again to join this stellar cast in Come From Away."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/17ecd7ce2bac5d3d",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Jessica-Gallant-Headshot-2025_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Jessica Gallant"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: 10th Season. Becoming Dolly (Creator/Dolly); I&rsquo;m Every Woman, Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade; (Anne Shirley); Mamma Mia!, Evangeline, Alice Through the Looking Glass, Canada Rocks!, 2010/2012 Young Company.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE (select): Anna in Frozen, Freaky Friday (Theatre Aquarius); Alice in Wonderland (Bad Hats/Soulpepper); Aphrodite in Mythic (Segal Centre).\r\n\r\nFILM/TV: Tell Me Lies (HULU); The Miniature Wife (Peacock); Accused (FOX/Sony).\r\n\r\nOTHER: Jessica received the King Charles III Coronation Medal of Honour for her contribution to the Arts in Prince Edward Island.\r\n\r\n&ldquo;A proud Islander! Thrilled to be back on the stage that started it all. For my L&rsquo;s and Island family, always.&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG: @jessicagallant3"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/33050a0f5a055844",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/GARWOOD-TAYLOR-Headshot_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Taylor Garwood"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE (select): White Christmas (Shaw Festival); All the Cows are Dead, The Frogs, Into The Woods, Outheis (Talk is Free Theatre); A Christmas Carol (Tweed &amp; Co.); Mamma Mia! (Thousand Islands Playhouse); Uncovered: Fleetwood Mac &amp; The Eagles, Putting It Together, Get A Life: A Banks Prize Cabaret (The Musical Stage Company).\r\n\r\nTRAINING: Sheridan College.\r\n\r\n&ldquo;I have known Anne Shirley since I was very young, and she has had such an impact on who I&rsquo;ve grown up to be. I am so excited to step into her world this summer on beautiful PEI.&rdquo;”"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/9013132be952245d",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Kaleigh-Gorka-Headshot-2026_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kaleigh Gorka"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Anne of Green Gables—The Musical™, Jersey Boys.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Frozen (Theatre Aquarius); Frozen (Canadian Premiere), Rocky Horror, Peter Pan (Neptune Theatre); Jersey Boys (Thousand Islands Playhouse); Grease, Anne of Green Gables—The Musical™, Footloose (Drayton); Chris, Mrs. (Elgin); Rock of Ages (Mayfield); Camelot (VPP); Grease, Footloose (Chemainus); Charlotte (European Tour); HOTHOUSE (Premiere – Theatre Kingston).\r\n\r\nTRAINING: BFA Acting (Toronto Metropolitan University, formerly Ryerson).\r\n\r\nKaleigh is honoured to be donning puffed sleeves and hopping on the bicycle once again, with an all-star cast and creative team.\r\n\r\n“Love and ongoing thanks to 10 Talent, my parents, and Josh.”\r\n\r\nIG: @kaleigh.gorka"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/d869c69ad676c385",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Stephen_Guy-McGrath-2.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Stephen Guy-McGrath"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nMamma Mia!, Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;, Million Dollar Quartet, Spinning Yarns, Evangeline, Tell Tale Harbour\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nONCE, Tell Tale Harbour (Mirvish); Christmas Carol, Midsummer Night&rsquo;s Dream, As You Like It, Blink, Three Sisters (Soulpepper); Dear Santa, The Perils of Persephone, A Closer Walk with Patsy Cline, BULLY (Theatre Orangeville); God of Carnage (STC); No Great Mischief (Tarragon, Vancouver Playhouse, Neptune, GCTC); Tide &amp; Time (Foster Festival)\r\nFILM/TV:\r\nReign, Murdoch Mysteries, Borje, Coroner, Anne, Mayday, Stockholm\r\nTRAINING:\r\nNational Theatre School of Canada, Soulpepper Academy\r\n\r\n&ldquo;I am beyond thrilled to be playing Claude, the Mayor of Gander, a town less than an hour from my family&rsquo;s &lsquo;home town&rsquo; of Musgrave Hr., Newfoundland. This is a dream role 15 years in the making &mdash; I was asked to be in the original workshop but had a conflict, and now I am finally &lsquo;coming home&hellip; from away!&rsquo;&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@sgmplays"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/ca381d91b05aa99d",
