    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Catherine O&#8217;Brien"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nAnne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;, Hairspray, Buddy: The Buddy Holly Story, Separate Beds, The Ballad of Stompin&rsquo; Tom, Disco Cirque, British Invasion, Canada Rocks, Emily\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nAnne and Gilbert (The Guild); Grace and Glorie (PEIPWYC); Footloose, Wizard of Oz (Drayton Entertainment); Fascinating Ladies (Young at Heart Theatre)\r\n\r\nCatherine is the Artistic Director of Young at Heart Theatre on PEI, now in its 21st year. She also volunteers with local environmental groups, including the Coalition for the Protection of PEI Water.\r\n\r\n\r\nCatherine is delighted to be back with the Charlottetown Festival, working with amazing and dedicated artists from across Canada."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/41169f9ee57be238",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Drew-Plummer-Headshot-2026_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Drew Plummer"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nCharlottetown Festival Young Company (2016), Sobey Family Theatre Debut\r\nTHEATRE (SELECT):\r\nShrek the Musical (Drayton Entertainment); 9 to 5 – The Musical (Thousand Islands Playhouse); The Secret Garden, My Fair Lady, On the Razzle, Gypsy, White Christmas, A Year with Frog and Toad, Flush, Holiday Inn, Brigadoon (Shaw Festival); Grease – The Musical (Winter Garden Theatre); Mamma Mia! (Rainbow Stage)\r\n\r\n“Thank you to Talenthouse and the Charlottetown Festival for this special opportunity! What a dream it is to be back in one of the most beautiful cities in Canada! I am truly grateful to be joining this warm and generous cast to share in these incredible stories with all of you. Thank you for supporting live theatre!”"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/0f4f84721038a0e2",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Pottle-Kristen-Headshot-2024-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kristen Pottle"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\n10 Seasons, 9 with Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;, Tell Tale Harbour, Jesus Christ Superstar, I&rsquo;m Every Woman\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nTell Tale Harbour (Mirvish); Wizard of Oz (Mirvish and US National Tour); West Side Story (Banff/Citadel Program and Vancouver Opera); Matilda, Newsies, Addams Family (Choreographer); Associate Artistic Director (Craig Fair Productions); Owner (Blossoming Heart Yoga)\r\n\r\n&ldquo;Always a joy to be back home in Avonlea. My 9th production and I somehow love it more each time. We couldn&rsquo;t have a better cast to do it with! This season is dedicated to my incredibly supportive family, to Simon, and to my favourite redhead, Clark.&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@blossomingheartyoga"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/7da454d66a654d4b",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Rollock-Shakeil-Headshot-2022.jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Shakeil Rollock"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nAnne of Green Gables—The Musical™, Tell Tale Harbour\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nGypsy, A Grand Night for Singing (Shaw Festival); Mary Poppins, Elf The Musical (The Grand); Fiddler on the Roof (Drayton Entertainment)\r\nFILM/TV:\r\nSneakerella, Spin (Disney+); Locke and Key, Grand Army (Netflix); American Gods (Amazon Prime)\r\nTRAINING:\r\nYork University, The School of Toronto Dance Theatre\r\n\r\nI’m beyond grateful to have another beautiful season on the Island.\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@shakroll"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/f131f401297e4180",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Julia-Swartrz-Headshot-2026_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Julia Schwartz"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDebut\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nThe Little Mermaid, Aladdin (Disney Cruise Line); Heathers: The Musical, Big Fish, Armchair Confidential, Piper (Sheridan College); Something Rotten (Theatre Under the Stars)\r\nTRAINING:\r\nHonours Bachelor of Music Theatre Performance (Sheridan College)\r\n\r\nJulia would like to thank all her family, friends, and the team at Talent House for their constant support in her life. She could not have done this without them and hopes you enjoy the show!\r\n\r\n\r\n&ldquo;I am so excited to be making my Charlottetown Festival debut this year in Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade; as Ruby! It is an honour to be working on this true Canadian classic alongside such an amazing creative team and cast, and I can&rsquo;t wait to enter the world of Avonlea to share this heartfelt story.&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@juliaschwartz.mp4"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/be982a6aaaee048f",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/BerkleySilvermanHeadshot.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Berkley Silverman"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nRide: The Musical (Canadian Premiere) (WJT); Bring it On! (Globe Theatre); Beetlejuice (NCL); The 25th Annual Putnam County Spelling Bee (Shifting Ground Collective); Fiddler on the Roof, Evita, Shrek, The Prom (Drayton Entertainment); Blocked (TheaterWorks USA); Drama 101 (Toronto Fringe); Innocence Lost (Soulpepper); The Hockey Sweater (Segal Centre)\r\nFILM/TV (SELECT):\r\nPaw Patrol (Nickelodeon); Reverse 1999 (OneLine Studios); Murdoch Mysteries (CBC/UKTV); Abducted on Prom Night (Lifetime); Workin’ Moms (Netflix); Cross (Amazon Prime)\r\nBerkley is absolutely thrilled to be making her Charlottetown Festival debut as Anne in Anne of Green Gables—The Musical™! She is deeply honoured to get to bring one of the most iconic Canadian stories to life.\r\n\r\n“Huge thanks to Ros, Steven, my NY team, TDZ, AMI, and my family and friends. Emma, I couldn’t do this without your support. I love you so much. Biggest love goes to my incredible mom, who inspires me every day and makes my dreams a reality.”\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@BerkleySilverman"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/bef8ba328a416522",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Calvert-Robin-Headshot-2025-scaled.jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Robin Calvert"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\n21 Seasons. Anne of Green Gables—The Musical™, Tell Tale Harbour, I’m Every Woman (Director/Choreographer), Kronborg\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nCinderella—The Ross Petty Panto (Elgin Theatre); HMS Pinafore (Assistant Choreographer) (Stratford Festival); Christmas Story: The Musical, Hairspray, Belly Full, Freaky Friday, Sound of Music, Legally Blonde (Theatre Aquarius); The Full Monty, Rock of Ages, Vegas Live, Mamma Mia! (Mayfield); Bitter Girl, The Little Mermaid, Rock of Ages, Beauty and the Beast, The Drowsy Chaperone (Drayton Entertainment)\r\nOTHER:\r\nCo-creator of In Thy Name as part of the Stratford Festival Lab\r\n\r\n“Coming home to Anne for my 22nd season at The Charlottetown Festival is truly special. You are about to experience the beautiful story of Anne once again through the heart, spirit, and imagination of our incredible company of actors. Many thanks to Talent House, and all my love always to Mom, Gabe, and Kitty. ‘Kindred spirits are not so scarce as I used to think.’ — Anne of Green Gables”\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@robincalvert29"
      }
    ]
  },
