      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDear Rita, Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;, Between Breaths\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nShrek: The Musical, Charlie and the Chocolate Factory (YPT); Natasha, Pierre, and the Great Comet of 1812 (Crow&rsquo;s/Mirvish); A Strange Loop (Soulpepper); Robin Hood: A Very Merry Family Musical, The Wizard of Oz: A Holiday Pantomime (Canadian Stage); La Cage aux Folles (Stratford Festival); Fall on Your Knees (Vita Brevis); Kelly vs Kelly (Musical Stage); After the Rain (Tarragon/Musical Stage)\r\nTRAINING:\r\nThe National Theatre School of Canada and Sheridan College\r\n\r\nBrian is a designer for theatre from Newfoundland and Labrador who currently resides in Bathurst, New Brunswick and a proud member of IATSE659 &ndash; The Associated Designers of Canada."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/1b36b9279bf838ab",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Cory-Sincennes-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Cory Sincennes"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nAnne of Green Gables—The Musical™, Evangeline, Jesus Christ Superstar, Mamma Mia!\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nWaiting for Godot, The Importance of Being Earnest (Stratford Festival); Anything Goes, Gypsy, Prince Caspian, Damn Yankees (Shaw Festival); Vinyl Cafe, Frozen, Shakespeare in Love, Matilda, Three Musketeers, Spamalot! (Citadel Theatre); The Secret Garden, The Louder We Get, Billy Elliot, Bad Jews, Liberation Days (Theatre Calgary); Next to Normal, Mary Poppins, Crazy for You (Theatre Calgary/Citadel Theatre)\r\nTRAINING:\r\nMFA in Theatre Design (University of Alberta)\r\nCory is an award-winning designer, currently residing in Charlottetown, PEI. His designs have received both national and international recognition, having worked throughout Canada, Europe, and Russia.\r\nWEB:\r\n\r\ncorysincennes.com"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/de83ebb056e23058",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Bob-Foster-headshot.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Robert Foster"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nJersey Boys, MAGGIE, Tell Tale Harbour, Million Dollar Quartet, Mamma Mia!, Evangeline, Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;\r\nTHEATRE (SELECT):\r\nCome From Away, The Wizard of Oz, Billy Elliot, Rock of Ages, Hairspray, Dirty Dancing, The Boys in the Photograph (Mirvish); Wild Party, Passing Strange (Acting Up Stage); Peter Pan, Snow White, Robin Hood, Cinderella (Ross Petty Productions); Batboy: The Musical, Evita, Camelot, Little Shop of Horrors (MTC/Theatre Calgary); Twist and Shout, Legends (Drayton); Into the Woods, Fire (Theatre Calgary)\r\n\r\nBob co-wrote the songs &ldquo;Good Mother&rdquo; and &ldquo;Looking for It&rdquo; with Jann Arden and played for years with her live and in studio. He is the recipient of two SOCAN Airplay Awards and two Betty Mitchell Awards."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/37e4039d42fa0b7a",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/kat-headshot.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kat Chin"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDebut\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nPell&eacute;as et M&eacute;lisande; The Magic Flute plus fourteen other productions (Opera Atelier); Aportia Chryptych: A Black Opera for Portia White (Canadian Opera Company); Hansel &amp; Gretel: A Sticky &amp; Sweet Panto; Rez Gas; Steel Magnolias (Capitol Theatre); Alice in Wonderland (Bad Hats); I am William (Stratford Festival)\r\nFILM/TV:\r\n21 Black Futures (CBC)\r\nTRAINING:\r\nRyerson Theatre School\r\n\r\nBased in Toronto, Kat has worked across Canada, Off-Broadway, and at the Palace of Versailles in France. She has been a member of the CAEA SM Committee since 2013, has taught at Toronto Metropolitan University, the SMArts Conference, and coaches at the National Theatre School.\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@bitwhizzle"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/fd861cc4b6ea2c15",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Ada-Aguilar-Headshot-2025.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ada Aguilar"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDebut\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nAs I Must Live It (TPM); Rez Gas (Cameco Capitol); Life After (Yonge Street Theatricals/Mirvish); Table for Two, 88 Keys, August Osage County, Noises Off (Soulpepper); Rosmersholm, Wedding Party (Crow’s); Into the Woods (TIFT); 1939 (Stratford Festival); The Runner (Human Cargo); School Girls; or, The African Mean Girls Play (Obsidian/Nightwood); Munschtime! (YPT)\r\nTRAINING:\r\nGlendon College, York University\r\n\r\n“Thank you for trusting me. Very excited to be spending a golden summer with this stellar Stage Management team and cast!”\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@biker_SM"
      }
    ]
  },
