    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Summer Camps"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Confederation Centre of the Arts Summer Camps are creative, immersive arts experiences for children and youth aged 5–17 throughout July and August. Designed to foster a love and understanding of different art forms, our programs go beyond typical summer activities by combining expert instruction, professional arts exposure, and creative community. Our summer camps provide: 🎨 Enriching arts-led learning in a supportive, structured environment tailored to inspire creativity, confidence, and artistic skill development. 👩‍🏫 Experienced teaching artists with Vulnerable Sector clearance who bring real-world expertise and mentorship to every session. 🖼️ Access to dedicated arts facilities and resources, providing campers with space and tools to explore visual arts, theatre, dance and music. 🎭 Opportunities to learn from and interact with arts professionals, including guest artists and industry practitioners. 🖼️ Weekly cultural outings, such as visits to the Confederation Centre Art Gallery and a matinee performance at the Charlottetown Festival, to broaden creative perspectives and link classroom learning with live cultural experiences. 👪 Showcases for families at the end of each week, giving campers a chance to display their work and celebrate their achievements with loved ones. Exploring Performing Arts Musical Theatre Intensive Exploring Visual Arts (FULL) These camp experiences are ideal [&hellip;]"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/keywords": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Arts Academy, Camps, Summer Camps"
      }
    ],
