    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ryan Abdullah Hooper"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDebut\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nThe Band’s Visit (Winnipeg Jewish Theatre); The Green Line (Downstage &amp; Chromatic Theatre); Brown Eyes: A New Musical (Workshop; TIFT); Cabaret, To Ronnie With Love, TomorrowLove (Theatre Sheridan)\r\nFILM/TV:\r\nAfter Love (Gearshift Films)\r\nTRAINING:\r\nHonours Bachelor of Music Theatre Performance (Sheridan College)\r\n\r\n“Lots of love to my amazing family and friends for all of their support!”\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@TheRyanHooper"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/7a65b84dc2c7bafa",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Lisa-MIchelle-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Lisa Michelle"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Debut.\r\nTHEATRE: Disney’s The Lion King (Mirvish Productions), Come From Away (Arts Club), Godspell (North American Tour/Drayton Ent), Avenue Q (Sudbury Theatre); Obeah Opera (Nightwood Theatre, BCurrent).\r\nFILM &amp; TV: Robyn Hood (Global TV), Murdoch Mysteries (CBC), Chucky (SyFy), Star Trek: Short Treks (Paramount+), A Sisterly Christmas (OWN Network), Hudson &amp; Rex (CTV).\r\nOTHER: Lisa Michelle is a two-time Canadian Screen Award nominee, an Artist Career Coach and mother to the best 11-year old in the universe. Infinite thanks to her husband, family &amp; friends for their endless support of her dreams!"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/21d9135da0d4b4fa",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Luc-Trottier-Headshot_.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Luc Trottier"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: Becoming Dolly (Director). THEATRE: Disney's The Lion King (Mirvish); A Midsummer Night's Dream (Theatre Orangeville), Grease (Elgin &amp; Winter Garden), Perry Loved Mary (Creator). FILM/TV: The Community Players (Creator/Bell Fibe); Interview With The Vampire (AMC), Vought Rising (Amazon Prime); Murdoch Mysteries (CBC);\r\nAmerican Gods (Starz); The Handmaid's Tale (MGM/Hulu); Suits (USA/Netflix). TRAINING: Bachelor of Music Theatre Performance, Sheridan College;Writing &amp; Producing Television Graduate Program, Humber College; Shakespeare Performance, Royal Academy of Dramatic Art. Luc is grateful to be a part of this stellar company. He is the proud owner of Human Moves Media, a PEI-based production company creating film, television, and theatre. For Lennon and Jessica, always! www.luctrottier.com \r\n\r\nQuote :  \r\n\r\nI am thrilled to be the Stand By for Claude, Oz, and Nick in one of the best Canadian musicals of all time Come From Away. From witnessing the very first workshop of\r\nCFA at Sheridan in 2012, to working as a Script Production Assistant on the pre-Broadway Toronto run in 2016, being cast in this production is a full circle moment!  \r\n\r\nInstagram : @luc_trottier  \r\n\r\nFacebook : https://www.facebook.com/luc.trottier \r\n\r\nwww.luctrottier.com "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/9839b7f90e1985ba",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/BrazierAdam-PreferredHeadshot.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Adam Brazier"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDirector: Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;, Jesus Christ Superstar, Mamma Mia!, Bittergirl, Jersey Boys, Million Dollar Quartet, Spinning Yarns and many more\r\nWRITING CREDITS:\r\nTell Tale Harbour, The Polkadot Door, The Munchables, Voices of Canada, Cinderella, Robin Hood, Aladdin, and Founding Father\r\n\r\nAs an actor, Adam has worked throughout Canada, Broadway, and London&rsquo;s West End. Adam&rsquo;s been nominated for Dora Awards as an actor, director, and producer."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/4e4c42153150ad51",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Jennifer-Mote.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Jen Mote"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDebut\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nCinderella (upcoming), Robin Hood, The Wizard of Oz (Canadian Stage); Rent (Stratford/Associate); Rock of Ages (Waitress #1/Mirvish); We Will Rock You (US National Tour)\r\nFILM/TV:\r\nChristmas in the Spotlight (Crave/Prime); The Wedding Planners (Prime)\r\n\r\n&ldquo;I&rsquo;m thrilled to be a part of this incredible team of cast and creatives, to help tell this beautiful story that celebrates empathy, generosity, and community.&rdquo;\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@jennifermote\r\n,\r\n\r\n@gloss_ent"
      }
    ]
  },
