  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/c298f1df4f8bdf87",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/RebekahBrownHeadshot.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Rebekah Brown"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "(she/her)\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Fiona - Shrek: the Musical (Capital Theatre); Anne Shirley - Anne &amp; Gilbert (Island Theatre Festival); Featured Performer - MUNSCHABLES (Confederation Centre of the Arts); Jo March - Little Women, Babekah - GODSPELL (8th Avenue) Players Lucinda - Into the Woods (The Guild); Heather Chandler - Heathers (Blackbox Theatre Co.) TV/FILM: Zoe - Cradle in the Waves, Julia - SeaSalt.\r\n\r\nSOCIAL MEDIA: IG @rebekahebrown09\r\n\r\nCOMING UP: You can see Rebekah in Stan Roger’s - Matter of Heart, Thunder Rolls - a Night of Garth Brooks and lots of other musical projects here in Charlottetown!"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/8d9f68001a78441f",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Julia.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Julia Cerisano"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nThe Creators Plan\r\n\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nMary Poppins, Little Women, Godspell (8th Avenue Players); Anne &amp; Gilbert (Island Theatre Festival); Storms A Brewin' (Feast Dinner Theatre); Heathers (Black Box Theatre Co.)\r\n\r\n“I'm so grateful to be returning to the Centre! I feel so blessed to be spending my summer doing what I love with amazing people. Enjoy the show!”\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@julia_cerisano"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/fbecbdf7b8e8e502",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/cat.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Cat Cummins"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nMunschables, The Creators Plan\r\n\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nAnne &amp; Gilbert (The Guild Theatre)\r\n\r\nTRAINING:\r\nCurrently studying Musical Theatre Performance (Sheridan College)\r\n\r\n“I’m so so so grateful to be back in my hometown doing what I love most! Big thanks to my family &amp; friends for all the love and support! Enjoy the show!”\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@cat_cummins24"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/8c58280a7b47cd38",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/kathleen.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kathleen Henthorn"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nAnne of Green Gables—The Musical™, Cinderella: A Fairly Tall Tale\r\n\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nThe Children’s Hour, Much Ado About Nothing (Theatre@York); The Witch of Edmonton: Staged Reading (Soulpepper); The Penelopiad, Concord Floral (York Studio Productions); Anne &amp; Gilbert, Beauty and the Beast (The Arts Guild)\r\n\r\nFILM/TV:\r\nSunshine on His Face, Edna (Film PEI &amp; Film4Ward)\r\n\r\nTRAINING:\r\nHonours BFA in Acting and Performance (York University)\r\n\r\nKathleen is thrilled to return to her home, Prince Edward Island, to join the Young Company after just completing her Acting degree in Toronto. She first began performing as a Child of Avonlea at 9 years old in Anne of Green Gables at the Festival, so this is a full circle moment for her.\r\n\r\nShe is over the moon to get to learn, play, and grow with this fantastic team of creatives in the place she loves most! Love to her family and friends for their endless support!\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@kath1een_h"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/787658725adae17e",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Samel-Sunil_Headshot-May-2026-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Samel Sunil"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE: The Creator’s Plan, Munschables, Anne of Green Gables, Holiday Spectacular.\r\n\r\nTHEATRE: Next to Normal (Bowtie Productions); Little Women (8th Avenue Players); Newsies (Colonel Gray); Descendants (Havenwood).\r\n\r\nTRAINING: Music Theatre Performance (Sheridan); Vocal training with Marcus Nance. Acting training with Amir Haidar, Suzanne Bennett, and Robert Gontier.\r\n\r\nAWARDS: National Music Festival Emerging Artist, NATS National Finalist, Queen's Platinum Jubilee, and PEI Youth Talent winner.\r\n\r\n“I am excited to be back home on PEI, doing what I love with this beautiful cast and crew. Thank you for all your support and love.”\r\n\r\nIG: @samel_sunil"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/d6d3337c45d1f4c4",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Kaitlyn-Thompkins-.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kaitlyn Thompkins"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\n    Debut\r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    THEATRE:\r\n    S.T.O.P/Animal Farm (TOURCo); Something Missing (Unnatural Disaster Theatre); (Half!)Sisters (The Meeting)\r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    TRAINING:\r\n    BA in Theatre (Dalhousie Fountain School of Performing Arts)\r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    AWARDS:\r\n    Outstanding Original Script (Halifax Fringe 2025); Outstanding Direction (Halifax Fringe 2025)\r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    \r\n      “I am beyond excited to get a chance to spend my summer on the island! Thank you to every person who has helped me get here. I believe that theatre for young audiences is so important: it introduces children to the magic of theatre, and it allows older artists to return to the magic of childhood. I am so incredibly excited to create with an amazing group of artists, I am sure it will be magical!”\r\n    \r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    IG:\r\n    \r\n      @kaitlyn.thompkins_03"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/3e4fcdd4e9aecff1",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Ryan-Whitty-.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ryan Whitty"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDebut\r\n\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nBert (8th Ave); Tom Collins (ACT); Roy Gardener/Gilbert US (Island Theatre Festival)\r\n\r\nFILM/TV:\r\nThe Snake (Club Red Productions); Love in Ashes of Us (Sleepy Bear Productions)\r\n\r\nTRAINING:\r\nPrep Program (Sheridan College)\r\n\r\nRyan is excited to be involved in this year's Young Company production.\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@whittyryan"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/51a47e19072978f8",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/BrazierAdam-PreferredHeadshot.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Adam Brazier*"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nDirector: Anne of Green Gables&mdash;The Musical&trade;, Jesus Christ Superstar, Mamma Mia!, Bittergirl, Jersey Boys, Million Dollar Quartet, Spinning Yarns and many more\r\nWRITING CREDITS:\r\nTell Tale Harbour, The Polkadot Door, The Munchables, Voices of Canada, Cinderella, Robin Hood, Aladdin, and Founding Father\r\n\r\nAs an actor, Adam has worked throughout Canada, Broadway, and London&rsquo;s West End. Adam&rsquo;s been nominated for Dora Awards as an actor, director, and producer."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/a4e58fd958c79277",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Morgan-Saulnier.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Morgan Saulnier"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\nJesus Christ Superstar, Tell Tale Harbour, Jersey Boys, Mamma Mia!, Alice Through the Looking Glass, I’m Every Woman, Maggie, Munschables\r\n\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nSongs for a New World, The Princess and the Handmaiden (Kitbag Theatre); Into the Woods in Concert, The Happy Prince, Anne and Gilbert (The Guild); Associate Music Director for Craig Fair Productions\r\n\r\nTRAINING:\r\nMasters of Music in Performance (Memorial University of Newfoundland), Bachelor of Music (University of Prince Edward Island)\r\n\r\nMorgan is the principal flautist for the University of Prince Edward Island Symphony Orchestra, and a sessional instructor in the University of Prince Edward Island music department.\r\n\r\n“I am so excited to be a part of the magic-making that is live theatre!”\r\n\r\nIG:\r\n\r\n@mlsaulnier"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/297e855659b1316b",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Holly.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Holly Meyer-Dymny"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTER:\r\nDebut\r\n\r\nTHEATRE:\r\nThe Wizard of Oz, The Full Monty, A Midsummer Night’s Dream (Neptune Theatre); The Wizard of Oz, The Music Man (Stage Prophets); Winter Moons (Nestuit’asi Storytelling); Dance Nation (Keep Good/HEIST); In My Own Little Corner (EveryBODY on Stage); The Wind in the Willows (Two Planks and a Passion); Into The Woods (The Grand Theatre); Angel’s Bone (Sound The Alarm, Loose Tea); Llandovery Castle (Opera Laurier), La Traviata (Loose Tea Musical Theatre)\r\n\r\nHolly Meyer-Dymny is an award-winning theatre designer, artist, mentor, and educator. They create Set, Lighting, and Projection Designs for theatre, dance, opera, musical theatre, and beyond.\r\n\r\nThey are a proud board member of the Associated Designers of Canada. They are delighted to be joining the team for Polka Dot Door.\r\nWEB:\r\n\r\nhollymeyerdymny.com"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/genid/7f22b162608ce6f0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/olena.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Olena Polyvach"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FOR THE CENTRE:\r\n    The Creator’s Plan (Stage Manager)\r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    THEATRE:\r\n    Fairytale of New York (Feast Dinner Theatre); Anne and Gilbert (Anne and Gilbert Inc); Elf The Musical (Revolution Dance Studio); Annie Jr. and Fame Jr. (Director)(Broadway Kids Studio); Shrek The Musical, Seussical Jr., Matilda Jr., Wizard of Oz (Managing Director)(Havenwood Dance Studio); Singer with Retro Party PEI\r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    TRAINING:\r\n    Masters, Television Directing. Broadway Teachers Workshop (MTI) 2020, 2022. Backstage Training at Stage Management, Props.\r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    \r\n      “Let’s Create some magic!”\r\n    \r\n  \r\n\r\n  \r\n    IG:\r\n    \r\n      @retropartypei\r\n    \r\n    \r\n\r\n    WEB:\r\n    \r\n      olenapolyvach.com"
      }
    ]
